text:
@rj_trading1 That's an ETHUSD Perp. That has $170M volume vs the $4.8B of ETHUSDT on Bybit today alone.

It's not the main pair and therefore not worth watching.

As far as I can see all the main ETHUSDT perps and spot pairs swept the low.

@misconfig_exe Both are bad.

But this time they don’t even believe their own scams/ponzi’s lol. Now it’s just instant extraction.

I guess this is worse short term, better long term seeing how Luna/FTX ended

@0RN0IR Lmao it would definitely be entertaining.

But yea, if the hackers sell the same amount or swap it to BTC or whatever then we wouldn't see much of a difference.

Would be interesting to know specifics on the details of the bridge loan but I don't think we'll get those

@zackvoell It's the wallet that's in between a hot and a cold one.

Not quite either of them, but still a bit warm.

What this means in terms of security and storage... I have no idea.

@imranMD09 I think we got over 100% but it was valued at the time of them going down.

For me there were just some stables on there so no issue.

But if you held for example $BTC which has done like a 6x from that point, you'll still only get the value it was at the time.

@dave_papers Even with those fees were much higher back then.

But yea some of it is definitely on L2s.

But with fees like these, I doubt many of the L2s are necessary (which was obvious already).

@Farrell1805 Well, we don't know what the tariffs will be and on which countries.

So can't properly price it in. Could have been an overreaction already or could not have been.

Generally I do think tariff dips should be pretty short though (at least in stocks).

@smw000001 @CryptoJelleNL Is it?

I just went with some reddit post which said it was around 400K in the picture.

Regardless, a ton of people haha

@anunnacapital There's also gaps at 3K, 9K etc.

They don't matter if price is trading miles away from it.

They can be good to watch if we're in somewhat of a close proximity <10% and ideally <2%

@Drewzillla Looks good to me here but we need a solid daily close imo.

But we took out a good amount of leverage and BTC had a nice reaction from FOMC so far,

But will remain volatile for a while here

@Tim_4444 Yep I'm mostly chilling as well :) 

Market testing everyone's patience yet again.

Glad you like it Tim, appreciate your content as well 👍

@HuyDrift 1. When you can change your life

Alternatively there are some good high timeframe tool/indicators like Pi Cycle top, puell multiple etc.

Additional to just crazy mania/overheated funding rates/parabolic charts for weeks on end

@BoardInvestor Generally think CME chop has a good chance.

But seeing we’re close to all time high/price discovery the odds of that happening do go down.

So answer is: Yes, but not as likely as usual. So not trading it personally

@BoardInvestor Yea probably.

Going to be great for this cycle. Not so much longer term if it means inflation resurfaces.

But hey, that's an issue for another day

@CryptoMutant I'm comparing the top 2 as they are miles above anything else.

Anything smaller/further down the risk curve will usually outperform on the upside.

Risk adjusted is what matters in the end

@GStoicCapital Where do I recommend anything.

I simply said what my base portfolio consists of. No recommendation anywhere.

I would argue that if there is a time for alts to shine against BTC it would be 2025 yes.

@GStoicCapital BTC is still up 6x from the lows.

That’s more than 99% of the small/mid caps people have been holding because they think BTC doesn’t yield them enough.

Big gains are made on alts yes. But most people don’t outperform BTC and underestimate how quick a few 5xes can compound.
